{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564531-session-2-of-the-thin-blood-hunt-first-time-story-teller-and-group","id":1564531,"title":"Session 2 of the thin blood hunt (first time story teller and group)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-10-05T07:18:39-07:00","id":1564531,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon7.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Session 2 of the thin blood hunt (first time story teller and group)","content":"Another month? Another list of funny things my new vampires keep doing:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>After 40 minutes of joking and summarizing the previous session and laying down a lot of our info- The team decides to infiltrate the Hospital where the thinblood ran from somehow to get patient and staff records.</li> <li>The Tremere surprisingly offers to use his mentor connections to try and get fake press badges and ID's for the group. The Venture surprise surprise decides to be the student journalist inquiring about the day in the life of a Hospital security guard. Our Nosforatu sits quietly in the corner for maybe an hour before coming up with the whimsical idea to sneak in via the laundry intake</li> <li><b>The entire group miscommunicates </b><i><u>(this will be important for later)</u></i></li> <li>The Nosfuratu intentionally soils a sheet to wear to better fit into her &quot;laundry&quot; ghillie suit role</li> <li>The gang drives out to do their business-</li> <li>The Tremere is dropped off at his Mentor's closed Pediatrics practice and has a nice chat about the things lost with their new life</li> <li>Our Venture and Nossy realize that they wont GET the passes and badges for the mission by tonight and that our Nossy has been totting around the now named &quot;poop blanket&quot; for hours making the car REEK.</li> <li>They decide to Visit the Press office that printed the &quot;escaped burn victim story&quot;. In a coincidence of great writing, the receptionist, whom has been noted as &quot;Hating people who smell bad&quot;, refuses to be near the front desk and gives our now shit smelling Venture the runaround about talking to the journalist responsible for the story.</li> <li>Her dominate attempt fails</li> <li>meanwhile Our Tremere tries using Auspex 3 times. Each a failure</li> <li>His third failure is a 1 and he goes catatonic for 5 minutes as a firetruck passes by and deafens his senses with its horn.</li> <li>Our tremere wakes up and decides with 5 computer pips to write a CD virus to backdoor the hospital servers (lol wait till he finds out its 1990)</li> <li><u><b>In grabbing a CD stack to burn he is noticed by a Hunter at the local Radioshack </b></u></li> <li>Our Venture is told to meet at a local coffee shop by the Journalist and is subsequently stood up but given his number by his colleague. She calls him and obtains some name and story info on the thin blood situation.</li> <li>Our Venture heads to the NEWARK NATIONAL AIRPORT of all places where a known Venture hangout happens to be the AMEX AMERICAN EXPRESS PREMIUM LOUNGE TRADEMARK. Here she attempts to link up with a few Gossip networks</li> <li>Our Nosforatu heads back to The Ventrue's apartment to just kick it for a while,</li> </ol>Somehow this takes from 12 to 5pm and everyone is REALLY excited over learning not much at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29128-internetflexing","name":"Internetflexing","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-05T12:52:51-07:00","id":1564549,"title":"","content":"How did he grab a stack of CDs in 1990?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T02:25:06-07:00","id":1564556,"title":"","content":"Using a premium airport lounge as a vampire hangout is a pretty clever idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T05:41:15-07:00","id":1564557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564531-session-2-of-the-thin-blood-hunt-first-time-story-teller-and-group?p=1564549#post1564549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did he grab a stack of CDs in 1990?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a REAL nice Radioshack and the tremere is rich. Probably how he got spotted by the pimply faced RadioShack employee Hunter. He flashed cash and asked to speak to the manager. I'll just say the stack was most likely 3 disks and cost 10k.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29128,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29128-internetflexing","user":"Internetflexing","date":". 10-06-2026, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29128-internetflexing","name":"Internetflexing","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T05:42:05-07:00","id":1564558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564531-session-2-of-the-thin-blood-hunt-first-time-story-teller-and-group?p=1564556#post1564556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using a premium airport lounge as a vampire hangout is a pretty clever idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I legit just wanted a fun place that wasn't a bar or opera house to use that was unique. I couldn't find out if they had such a lounge back in 1990 but the opportunity arose. Place has booths with small swinging doors too for &quot;privacy&quot; and low lighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29128-internetflexing","name":"Internetflexing","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T09:35:29-07:00","id":1564564,"title":"","content":"I liked the lounge idea too, intend to copy it and those exist since 1939 IRL, so fair to have one so exclusive in the game.<br /> <br /> Personally I don't like to let players make mistakes that really don't make sense for the characters, just because they don't live I'm that time. So I'd at least inform that the hospital is unlikely to have a CD reader to begin with. And I know many players would definitely not like this take.<br /> <br /> But I'm also aware a lot of groups have a blast with those, so you know your players. 10k is too much even being rare, I'd say a CD-ROM in 1990 exactly would cost between 50c and USD 5. 10\u00d7 more expensive than they would be some years later, but being cheap was part of the point.<br /> <br /> You'll have enough of an effect with the Tremere realizing that no money will summon more than 3 or so discs without a factory order that will take days at best to deliver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T12:12:54-07:00","id":1564569,"title":"","content":"the net was giving me odd prices but a BURNABLE CD in 1990 would be a professional item sold specialty- costing 70 to 90 a piece. So if they did have a &quot;stack&quot; it might be near 1k. CD readers on computers were becoming fairly common place by 1990 but a hospital would definitely be starting to change over to electronic data transfer in the city. My biggest goof for him will be that they would transfer employee data first, so the thin bloods records IF they have any would be physical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29128-internetflexing","name":"Internetflexing","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T13:12:59-07:00","id":1564570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Internetflexing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564531-session-2-of-the-thin-blood-hunt-first-time-story-teller-and-group?p=1564569#post1564569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the net was giving me odd prices but a BURNABLE CD in 1990 would be a professional item sold specialty- costing 70 to 90 a piece. So if they did have a &quot;stack&quot; it might be near 1k.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I could gather, the issue is more that integrated CD burners aren't a thing yet. Wikipedia had the rather evocative though unsourced description of CD burners in 1990 being &quot;washing machine sized&quot;. From the one picture I found of such a machine that seems a bit of an understatement.<br /> <br /> Maybe more to the point, in 1990 you'd just use a floppy disk. Ubiquitous, rewritable, and they would indeed sell them at Radioshack.<br /> <br /> That said if you're wedded to CDs, you're only a few years out. Could slap a Pentex logo on any technology that's slightly anachronistic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> CD readers on computers were becoming fairly common place by 1990... </div> </div> </div>Ubiquity is more of a 1994 thing. They were still really pretty expensive and as extremely new technology, there wasn't necessarily that much you could do with one yet. Like Windows 3.1 is going to be released in 1992 on floppy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but a hospital would definitely be starting to change over to electronic data transfer in the city. My biggest goof for him will be that they would transfer employee data first, so the thin bloods records IF they have any would be physical. </div> </div> </div>If you want that real '90s vibe, give them a green screen dinosaur from the '80s with a dot matrix printer. Like, a hospital needs their IT to be reliable not cutting edge, so using old technology makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T15:27:52-07:00","id":1564573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Internetflexing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564531-session-2-of-the-thin-blood-hunt-first-time-story-teller-and-group?p=1564569#post1564569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CD readers on computers were becoming fairly common place by 1990 but a hospital would definitely be starting to change over to electronic data transfer in the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>1990 flat? No.<br /> <br /> In 1990 they were feasible to buy, not common. And not standard in business.<br /> <br /> By 1991 to 1993 a PC with CD driver was the equivalent of a gamer PC. Somewhere in 1994 they really went common and depending on where you live it became standard between 1995 and 1996.<br /> <br /> And businesses acquire hardware based on utility, not generic specs. Until 1997 you would only see games or extremely specific software in CDs, they were mostly for music. A hospital wouldn't have anything that requires more than a stack of floppy disks.<br /> <br /> Hospitals tend by the way to be quite resistant to change regular hardware. By 1990 you could expect a regular hospital to be using hardware acquired in 1980 already at the end of their commercial life. They will buy better where it is really necessary, because the computer is not a main asset. In 1990 almost nothing in the best hospitals required much more than a 1970's machine, they were just so old that their maintenance was expensive.<br /> <br /> Then we get to CD burners. Those weren't just really expensive: they were specialized to use and in short supply for a bulk buyer. For a user that means one big expense and learning the ropes. For a company that means buying bulk, scaling maintenance and substitutions, hiring or training personnel with higher paychecks, and a lot of bureaucracy to keep track of new and valuable equipment.<br /> <br /> So no, the hospital would use floppy disks. The hospital would use floppy disks all the way to the mid to late 2000s and maybe later. Flying companies still use floppy disks. In 1990 the hospital would not have a single CD burner to use those CDs on.<br /> <br /> But to be clear: I'm only being overly specific. You won't have a serious anachronism if you do that. If you want to use the chronicle as an exploration of the period that's another thing, but it's yours to decide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-06T16:28:35-07:00","id":1564576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564531-session-2-of-the-thin-blood-hunt-first-time-story-teller-and-group?p=1564573#post1564573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1990 flat? No.<br /> <br /> In 1990 they were feasible to buy, not common. And not standard in business.<br /> <br /> By 1991 to 1993 a PC with CD driver was the equivalent of a gamer PC. Somewhere in 1994 they really went common and depending on where you live it became standard between 1995 and 1996.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I still remember 'floppies' and 'hard floppies' being a lot more common for school computers back in the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-07T14:11:13-07:00","id":1564595,"title":"","content":"People tend to get surprised with how old hardware is in most companies, but the reality is that even highly specialized software usually don't require much.<br /> <br /> This is somewhat changing now with AI, some companies need local hosting, nonnegotiable, then that means at least one server with specs to run their workflows. Hospitals are increasing their use of specialized AI (not the commercial stuff like ChatGPT), so this is a thing.<br /> <br /> Everything else? Even the most advanced tech only needs very basic programs that run in surprisingly low specs. A modern hospital with remote surgery robots can run in late 80's PCs smoothly, what will need better hardware will be, believe it, the reception desk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T06:54:12-07:00","id":1564610,"title":"","content":"Why not just dominate an employee to get the patient records.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T12:51:52-07:00","id":1564618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1564531-session-2-of-the-thin-blood-hunt-first-time-story-teller-and-group?p=1564610#post1564610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not just dominate an employee to get the patient records.</div> </div> </div> </div>shhh theyre learning!<br /> <br /> Also my venture tried this on a secretary at the newspaper and lost","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29128-internetflexing","name":"Internetflexing","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}